___NOTES___

GA4 Support Cookie Banner

What this tag does
- Sets the Consent Mode v2 default to denied for every storage type except
  security_storage, before any other tag runs.
- Reads the ccb_consent cookie and restores an earlier choice, so a returning
  visitor is not asked again and your tags get the state they gave.
- Loads the banner UI from https://dashboard.ga4support.nl, keyed on your account ID.

Where to place it
Fire this tag on the built-in "Consent Initialization - All Pages" trigger, once per
event. Any tag that needs consent should fire later than this one.

What it does not do
It does not add consent settings to your other tags. Google tags honour the Consent
Mode signal by themselves; a Meta pixel or a session recorder does not. For those, set
Advanced Settings -> Consent Settings -> Require additional consent on the tag itself.

The consent cookie name is fixed at ccb_consent. It is written by the banner script, so
there is nothing to configure and no way to get it wrong.
